Package: fullsampleDML
Type: Package
Title: Cross-Fitting-Free Debiased Machine Learning with Multiway Dependence
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Kaicheng", "Chen", email = "chenkaicheng@sufe.edu.cn",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Harold D.", "Chiang", email = "hdchiang@wisc.edu",
           role = "aut")
  )
Description: Implements full-sample debiased generalized method of moments
    estimation with user-supplied orthogonal scores, feasible one- or two-step
    weighting, and positive-semidefinite or inclusion-exclusion covariance
    estimators for an arbitrary number of clustering dimensions. Nuisance
    functions are fitted on the complete sample without DML cross-fitting.
    Optional helpers integrate cluster-aware tuning through 'mlr3'. The methods
    accompany Chen and Chiang (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2602.11333>.
License: MIT
URL: https://github.com/kaichengchen/fullsampleDML-r,
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.11333
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Suggests:
    glmnet,
    knitr,
    mlr3,
    mlr3learners,
    mlr3tuning,
    paradox,
    rmarkdown,
    rpart,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
